  "description": "How the binary's behavior is checked. The unit tests sit at the end of each module and run on macOS and Linux in CI (cargo test --workspace). Each test runs in a testkit::Sandbox: a private HOME and state file, and a bin directory that FDS_TOOLS points the absolute tool paths at, so ditto, xattr, lsof, ps, launchctl and the rest are shell-script fakes. Several compress and dedupe tests are compiled only off macOS and so run only on the Linux CI runner (see their entities). Run them as a non-root user, or the permission tests cannot fail the way they should. Run one with `cargo test -p free-disk-space <test name>` in macos/rust.",
